Usages:
  update_pattern: |
    A companion "Update" data class mirrors the entity's fields as nullable, defaulted-to-null
    properties, so a repository can apply a sparse partial update (only non-null fields are
    written) without callers constructing a full entity.

Annotations: |
  This cell holds the domain-level chapter entity, its partial-update counterpart, and the
  exception used when a manga has no chapters at all. It has no dependency on any other cell.

  Use `update_pattern` for `ChapterUpdate`.

---

"Chapter(id: Long, mangaId: Long, read: Boolean, bookmark: Boolean, lastPageRead: Long, dateFetch: Long, sourceOrder: Long, url: String, name: String, dateUpload: Long, chapterNumber: Double, scanlator: String?, lastModifiedAt: Long, version: Long, memo: JsonObject)":
  location: Chapter.kt
  annotations: |
    One chapter of one manga, merging locally-tracked reading state with source-provided
    chapter metadata.

    id: local database row id
    `mangaId`: id of the owning Manga
    `read`: whether the user has marked this chapter fully read
    bookmark: whether the user bookmarked this chapter
    `lastPageRead`: last page index the user was on, for resuming
    `dateFetch`: epoch millis this chapter's metadata was last fetched from the source
    `sourceOrder`: position of this chapter within the source's own chapter listing, used to
    order chapters when chapterNumber is not reliable
    url: the source-specific chapter URL/identifier used to re-fetch pages
    name: chapter title as provided by the source
    dateUpload: epoch millis the chapter was uploaded on the source, or -1 if unknown
    chapterNumber: parsed chapter number; a negative value means it could not be recognized
    scanlator: name of the scanlation/translation group, or null if the source doesn't provide one
    memo: source-specific extra metadata, opaque to the app

    Algorithm:
    1. isRecognizedNumber reports whether chapterNumber is a valid non-negative value
    2. copyFrom(other) overwrites only the source-supplied fields (name, url, dateUpload,
       chapterNumber, scanlator) from a freshly-fetched chapter, leaving user-owned state
       (`read`, bookmark, `lastPageRead`) untouched

  methods:
    "copyFrom(other: Chapter) -> updated:Chapter": |
      Return a copy with only the source-supplied fields (name, url, dateUpload,
      chapterNumber, scanlator) replaced by other's values; local reading-state fields are
      preserved from the receiver.
  properties:
    "isRecognizedNumber -> Boolean": |
      True when chapterNumber is zero or positive, i.e. the chapter number parser succeeded.

"ChapterUpdate(id: Long, mangaId: Long?, read: Boolean?, bookmark: Boolean?, lastPageRead: Long?, dateFetch: Long?, sourceOrder: Long?, url: String?, name: String?, dateUpload: Long?, chapterNumber: Double?, scanlator: String?, version: Long?, memo: JsonObject?)":
  location: ChapterUpdate.kt
  annotations: |
    Sparse partial update for a Chapter row: only non-null fields are written by the
    repository implementation. id is always required and identifies the target row.

    Use `update_pattern`.

"NoChaptersException()":
  location: NoChaptersException.kt
  annotations: |
    Thrown when a source's chapter list for a manga comes back empty where at least one chapter
    was expected, distinguishing "genuinely has zero chapters" call sites from a plain fetch
    failure.

